# The Peano natural numbers as a self-type, with addition defined by structural recursion, and arithmetic facts PROVED
# BY THE KERNEL (judge.ts) computing normal forms. Unlike the integer-literal facts elsewhere (checked by the decision
# procedures), these reduce `plus one one` to `two` through the derived computing eliminator and the termination-gated
# transparent definition of `plus`, then `calm` (definitional equality / reflexivity) discharges the equation. This is
# the dependent-proof path: a proof is the kernel checking two terms share a normal form. See
# note/library/seed/proof-checking/05-recommendation.md and 09-math-dsl-cheatsheet.md.

# A natural number: zero, or the successor of a natural.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# Addition by recursion on the first argument: 0 + b = b, and (succ a) + b = succ (a + b). The recursion descends on
# the matched predecessor, so it is verified terminating and registered transparent (the kernel unfolds it).
task plus
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        read b
    case succ
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            call plus
              read prior
              read b

# The small numerals, as successor towers.
task one
  like natural
  send back
    make succ
      bind prior
        make zero

task two
  like natural
  send back
    make succ
      bind prior
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero

task three
  like natural
  send back
    make succ
      bind prior
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero

# one plus one is two: the kernel reduces plus one one through the eliminator and recursion, and checks it equals two.
rule one-plus-one-is-two
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        call one
        call one
      call two
  calm

# two plus one is three.
rule two-plus-one-is-three
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        call two
        call one
      call three
  calm

# one plus two is three: addition reduces on the FIRST argument, so this exercises a different reduction path than
# two-plus-one, and still lands on three.
rule one-plus-two-is-three
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        call one
        call two
      call three
  calm

# zero is a left identity, concretely: zero plus three is three (the base case of the recursion).
rule zero-plus-three-is-three
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        make zero
        call three
      call three
  calm

# UNIVERSAL laws proved through the kernel, not just concrete instances. These are definitional: each side reduces to
# the same normal form FOR EVERY value of the bound variables, so `calm` discharges them. Genuine forall-theorems.

# Zero is a left identity for addition: 0 + n = n, for every natural n. (The zero branch of plus returns its second
# argument directly, so plus zero n reduces to n even when n is an arbitrary variable.)
rule plus-zero-left-is-identity
  mark n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        make zero
        read n
      read n
  calm

# The successor steps out of a sum: (succ a) + b = succ (a + b), for every a and b. (This is the recursion equation of
# plus, definitionally true.)
rule plus-succ-steps-out
  mark a, like natural
  mark b, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call plus
        make succ
          bind prior
            read a
        read b
      make succ
        bind prior
          call plus
            read a
            read b
  calm

# Multiplication by recursion on the first argument: 0 * b = 0, and (succ a) * b = b + (a * b). Recursion descends on
# the matched predecessor, so it is verified terminating and the kernel unfolds it.
task times
  take a, like natural
  take b, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read a
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      send back
        call plus
          read b
          call times
            read prior
            read b

# Zero is a left absorber for multiplication: 0 * n = 0, for every n. Definitional.
rule times-zero-left-is-zero
  mark n, like natural
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        make zero
        read n
      make zero
  calm

# A concrete product: two times two is four, computed through the kernel (multiplication unfolds into two additions).
rule two-times-two-is-four
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call times
        call two
        call two
      call plus
        call two
        call two
  calm
